<description>&lt;p&gt;Armed clashes persist in Bangui among government forces, former Séléka rebels, Anti-balaka militias, Russian Wagner troops and Africa Corps, while the United Nations warns against a premature peacekeeper withdrawal. Chad arrested four suspects after an attack in Miski, and CAR officials denied that their forces crossed the Chad border during a raid. Former hostages were released and greeted by President Touadéra in Bangui after returning from captivity. The conflict caused 246 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxORmhVRmhiOXFOc201Y0ZSRHF4UXU4TjQ1dElfbmJXUmlVdWV2anEzVHRiRjdXZFJrN2V5QWpFMURodU5DNG8tdThKYjFidVlVX2Z5a0RhaUtVSzd5M0V6WlB6MllyN3FlTHdnTzZMWVhJTG12eHpqd1gzX3ZwSlpvanVQb1lSY29FZGdjQzd4M0lQUWg4MFIxV2RJNUFEVHFBdlR0SnZhazVxZkwzc1RodQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Audacy&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimwFBVV95cUxNOGRsOTlRV3pTaV92dzlrNjdXWmJCZjlpT0wzaWE1cm9NeENuU3NFU0ZDcmdWNVJ3Z29GdWZFOWNtb2M1WExCOTdOUGUtTnFzWE9SeXEwOTNOcFkyaU5uajlFa0dUcHFYS3Q3VnNwbUNxOC1yRTM0LTJJVkFaQjg1SmlFRGtwYTlsRl84aXNLOWVleWJZbWI2STNZbw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Head Topics&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxPLTcxZHZKRFpQaDB6Qi00WHVzbWp2aFMzYVI2YkJOUWhmak11OHZCdGMzWFRsak5ybjNTcGZoc0QwY0hIdFhvUWI4emtQUXFyX2diSU8tdVkxMTd5UW9SNS11M0hXOTRfUFJ5VDBTNFdnNG1ZemRxT1FrbngtLUUtLUtuR0ZvNHZLZHNqYzNRQkY3SjRud1NadVBEbnljVnljcGZJT19VU1pVc1VHbmU4SExBRk9RM0VNeWJWN0xXeTk?oc=5&quot;&gt;GhanaWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitwFBVV95cUxNQjM1cVpSOVZPUkpUNlp6WnY3MUpBdW55UW94V2xYYmNXY3d2dVBiZURYSlFlTmxwM1FMY3d6dUxneTRjRGhYUGl4aDdRLVhuZ1ZjV0thSHBfNy03eUc5LW8weFlLTThZNEFkYUM2ZTd3dTVGdTlMNmMzSEtBempjNEp5ODZ1bkQzWVF